From 5dcab258c312eb87d544991a5fb42d53c940851e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:52:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] feat(content): set form values through the native value
 setter

React, Angular and Vue keep their own value tracker on inputs and
textareas. Assigning `element.value` updates that tracker before the
`input` event fires, so the framework sees no change and the field
silently reverts. Writing through the prototype setter bypasses the
tracker; the events that follow report a real change.

- Add src/content/native-value.ts with findNativeValueSetter and
  setNativeValue (native setter with plain-assignment fallback, then
  `input`/`change` by default; `blur` optional and non-bubbling).
- Use it in setFormValue (type --ref), smartType (type --into) and
  FORM_FILL (form.fill) for text inputs and textareas. Checkbox, radio,
  select and contenteditable paths are unchanged.
- Expose the same routine to `surf js` as piHelpers.setValue(el, value,
  events?).

